IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `epd-nouns`
IMPORT `epd-seat`

-- CASES for the individual's seat (epd-seat.l4). Every question has at least one case; the expected value of each was decided from the
-- text of the Directive before the run, and the reason is written above the assertion. Every call names its arguments.
-- JUST TRUE = the text says yes; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = the text does not answer.

§ `Is the Directive on this at all (Articles 1 to 3)?`
-- I1: Does the Directive apply to this activity (Art 1(3))?
-- State security is named in Art 1(3) as outside the Directive: "shall in no case apply to activities concerning ... State security".
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive apply to what is being done` WITH `the activity is outside the Treaty on the Community` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns public security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns defence` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns State security` IS TRUE, `the activity concerns the economic well-being of the State` IS FALSE, `the activity relates to State security matters` IS FALSE, `the activity is the State acting in criminal law` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Economic well-being of the State counts only "when the activities relate to State security matters": here they do not, so Art 1(3) is silent.
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive apply to what is being done` WITH `the activity is outside the Treaty on the Community` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns public security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns defence` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns State security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns the economic well-being of the State` IS TRUE, `the activity relates to State security matters` IS FALSE, `the activity is the State acting in criminal law` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Economic well-being when the activity relates to State security matters is excluded.
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive apply to what is being done` WITH `the activity is outside the Treaty on the Community` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns public security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns defence` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns State security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns the economic well-being of the State` IS TRUE, `the activity relates to State security matters` IS TRUE, `the activity is the State acting in criminal law` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- None of the exclusions: Art 1(3) says nothing either way.
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive apply to what is being done` WITH `the activity is outside the Treaty on the Community` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns public security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns defence` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns State security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns the economic well-being of the State` IS FALSE, `the activity relates to State security matters` IS FALSE, `the activity is the State acting in criminal law` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I2: Does the Directive apply to the processing of my personal data (Art 3)?
-- Personal data, public service, public network, in the Community: Art 3 says the Directive applies.
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive apply to the processing of my personal data` WITH `the processing is of my personal data` IS TRUE, `the processing is for a publicly available electronic communications service` IS TRUE, `the network is a public communications network` IS TRUE, `the network is in the Community` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Outside the Community: Art 3 is silent.
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive apply to the processing of my personal data` WITH `the processing is of my personal data` IS TRUE, `the processing is for a publicly available electronic communications service` IS TRUE, `the network is a public communications network` IS TRUE, `the network is in the Community` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I3: I am a company or other legal person: does the Directive protect my legitimate interests (Art 1(2))?
-- Art 1(2) second sentence: the Directive provides for protection of the legitimate interests of subscribers who are legal persons.
#ASSERT (`As a legal person do I have my legitimate interests protected by the Directive` WITH `I am a legal person` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A natural person: this sentence is silent about them.
#ASSERT (`As a legal person do I have my legitimate interests protected by the Directive` WITH `I am a legal person` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I4: Am I a "user" under the Directive (Art 2(a))?
-- A natural person using a publicly available service: Art 2(a) "means".
#ASSERT (`Am I a user under the Directive` WITH `I am a natural person` IS TRUE, `I use a publicly available electronic communications service` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not using such a service: not a user.
#ASSERT (`Am I a user under the Directive` WITH `I am a natural person` IS TRUE, `I use a publicly available electronic communications service` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I5: Is what happened to my data a "personal data breach" (Art 2(i))?
-- A breach of security leading to unauthorised access to personal data of a public service: Art 2(i) "means".
#ASSERT (`Is what happened to my data a personal data breach` WITH `there was a breach of security` IS TRUE, `my data was accidentally or unlawfully destroyed` IS FALSE, `my data was accidentally or unlawfully lost` IS FALSE, `my data was accidentally or unlawfully altered` IS FALSE, `my data was disclosed without authority` IS FALSE, `my data was accessed without authority` IS TRUE, `the data was personal data held for a public communications service in the Community` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A breach of security with none of the listed consequences is not a personal data breach.
#ASSERT (`Is what happened to my data a personal data breach` WITH `there was a breach of security` IS TRUE, `my data was accidentally or unlawfully destroyed` IS FALSE, `my data was accidentally or unlawfully lost` IS FALSE, `my data was accidentally or unlawfully altered` IS FALSE, `my data was disclosed without authority` IS FALSE, `my data was accessed without authority` IS FALSE, `the data was personal data held for a public communications service in the Community` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I6: Is this message "electronic mail" under the Directive (Art 2(h))?
-- A text message sent over a public network and stored until collected: Art 2(h) "means" (this covers short message service messages).
#ASSERT (`Is this message electronic mail under the Directive` WITH `it is a text, voice, sound or image message` IS TRUE, `it was sent over a public communications network` IS TRUE, `it stays stored until I collect it` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A live call that cannot be stored until collected is not electronic mail.
#ASSERT (`Is this message electronic mail under the Directive` WITH `it is a text, voice, sound or image message` IS TRUE, `it was sent over a public communications network` IS TRUE, `it stays stored until I collect it` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I7: Is what I did "consent" under the Directive (Art 2(f))?
-- Art 2(f): consent "corresponds to the data subject's consent in Directive 95/46/EC": the borrowed requirement is met.
#ASSERT (`Is what I did consent under the Directive` WITH `what I did is consent in the sense of Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The borrowed requirement is not met: not consent.
#ASSERT (`Is what I did consent under the Directive` WITH `what I did is consent in the sense of Directive 95/46/EC` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `My communications and my device (Article 5)`
-- I8: Must my communications and the related traffic data be kept confidential (Art 5(1))?
-- Art 5(1): Member States shall ensure the confidentiality of communications and related traffic data by those means.
#ASSERT (`Must my communications and traffic data be kept confidential` WITH `it is my communication or traffic data about it` IS TRUE, `it is by a public network or publicly available service` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A private network: the sentence is limited to public networks and publicly available services.
#ASSERT (`Must my communications and traffic data be kept confidential` WITH `it is my communication or traffic data about it` IS TRUE, `it is by a public network or publicly available service` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I9: Must the Member State prohibit this person from listening to or intercepting my communications (Art 5(1))?
-- Interception of my communications by a third party without my consent and without authority: prohibited.
#ASSERT (`Must this interception of my communications be prohibited` WITH `it is listening, tapping, storage, interception or surveillance` IS TRUE, `it is of my communications or related traffic data` IS TRUE, `it is by someone other than a user` IS TRUE, `I consented to it` IS FALSE, `it is legally authorised under Article 15(1)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I consented: the prohibition is "without the consent of the users concerned".
#ASSERT (`Must this interception of my communications be prohibited` WITH `it is listening, tapping, storage, interception or surveillance` IS TRUE, `it is of my communications or related traffic data` IS TRUE, `it is by someone other than a user` IS TRUE, `I consented to it` IS TRUE, `it is legally authorised under Article 15(1)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- "except when legally authorised to do so in accordance with Article 15(1)": the exception is met.
#ASSERT (`Must this interception of my communications be prohibited` WITH `it is listening, tapping, storage, interception or surveillance` IS TRUE, `it is of my communications or related traffic data` IS TRUE, `it is by someone other than a user` IS TRUE, `I consented to it` IS FALSE, `it is legally authorised under Article 15(1)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I10: Does the confidentiality rule stop my provider storing data that is technically needed to carry my communication (Art 5(1))?
-- "This paragraph shall not prevent technical storage which is necessary for the conveyance of a communication".
#ASSERT (`Does the confidentiality rule stop technical storage needed to carry my communication` WITH `the storage is technical and necessary for the conveyance` IS TRUE, `the storage is without prejudice to confidentiality` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Storage that is not needed to convey the communication: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`Does the confidentiality rule stop technical storage needed to carry my communication` WITH `the storage is technical and necessary for the conveyance` IS FALSE, `the storage is without prejudice to confidentiality` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I11: Does the confidentiality rule stop a business recording my call as evidence of a transaction (Art 5(2))?
-- A legally authorised recording in the course of lawful business practice to prove a transaction is not affected by Art 5(1).
#ASSERT (`Does the confidentiality rule stop a business recording my call as evidence` WITH `the recording is legally authorised` IS TRUE, `the recording is of communications and related traffic data` IS TRUE, `the recording is in the course of lawful business practice` IS TRUE, `the recording is to provide evidence of a business transaction` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A recording not legally authorised: the paragraph is silent.
#ASSERT (`Does the confidentiality rule stop a business recording my call as evidence` WITH `the recording is legally authorised` IS FALSE, `the recording is of communications and related traffic data` IS TRUE, `the recording is in the course of lawful business practice` IS TRUE, `the recording is to provide evidence of a business transaction` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I12: Is storing information on my device, or reading what is on it, allowed only with my consent (Art 5(3))?
-- Art 5(3): storing or access in a subscriber's or user's terminal equipment "is only allowed on condition that" consent is given.
#ASSERT (`Is storing information on my device or reading it allowed only with my consent` WITH `it is storing, or gaining access to, information in my device` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not storing or accessing information in the terminal equipment: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`Is storing information on my device or reading it allowed only with my consent` WITH `it is storing, or gaining access to, information in my device` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I13: Was the condition of consent met for what was stored on, or read from, my device (Art 5(3))?
-- Consent, clear and comprehensive information, in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC: the condition is met.
#ASSERT (`Was the condition of consent met for what was stored on or read from my device` WITH `I gave consent` IS TRUE, `I was given clear and comprehensive information` IS TRUE, `the consent and information meet Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No clear and comprehensive information: "only allowed on condition that" consent has been given with that information.
#ASSERT (`Was the condition of consent met for what was stored on or read from my device` WITH `I gave consent` IS TRUE, `I was given clear and comprehensive information` IS FALSE, `the consent and information meet Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I14: Does the consent rule stop storing or access on my device that is strictly necessary for a service I asked for (Art 5(3))?
-- Technical storage strictly necessary for a service the user explicitly requested: not prevented.
#ASSERT (`Does the consent rule stop storage on my device strictly necessary for a service I asked for` WITH `it is technical storage or access` IS TRUE, `it is for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication` IS FALSE, `I explicitly asked the service provider for the service` IS TRUE, `it is strictly necessary for that provider to give me the service` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not strictly necessary and not for the sole purpose of transmission: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`Does the consent rule stop storage on my device strictly necessary for a service I asked for` WITH `it is technical storage or access` IS TRUE, `it is for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication` IS FALSE, `I explicitly asked the service provider for the service` IS TRUE, `it is strictly necessary for that provider to give me the service` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `My traffic data (Article 6)`
-- I15: Must my provider now erase my traffic data or make it anonymous (Art 6(1))?
-- "must be erased or made anonymous when it is no longer needed for the purpose of the transmission of a communication".
#ASSERT (`Must my provider erase my traffic data or make it anonymous` WITH `it is traffic data about me held by my provider` IS TRUE, `my provider no longer needs it to carry my communication` IS TRUE, `another rule lets my provider keep it` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Still needed for the transmission: "when it is no longer needed" is not met.
#ASSERT (`Must my provider erase my traffic data or make it anonymous` WITH `it is traffic data about me held by my provider` IS TRUE, `my provider no longer needs it to carry my communication` IS FALSE, `another rule lets my provider keep it` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "without prejudice to paragraphs 2, 3 and 5 ... and Article 15(1)": what those allow is not decided here.
#ASSERT (`Must my provider erase my traffic data or make it anonymous` WITH `it is traffic data about me held by my provider` IS TRUE, `my provider no longer needs it to carry my communication` IS TRUE, `another rule lets my provider keep it` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I16: May my provider still process my traffic data for billing on this date (Art 6(2))?
-- Within the period during which the bill may lawfully be challenged or payment pursued.
#ASSERT (`May my provider still process my traffic data for billing on this date` WITH `it is data needed for billing and interconnection payments` IS TRUE, `the date of the processing` IS (Date 10 1 2025), `the last day my bill can be challenged or payment pursued` IS (Date 31 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "only up to the end of the period": the day after the last day is outside it.
#ASSERT (`May my provider still process my traffic data for billing on this date` WITH `it is data needed for billing and interconnection payments` IS TRUE, `the date of the processing` IS (Date 1 2 2025), `the last day my bill can be challenged or payment pursued` IS (Date 31 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I17: May my provider process my traffic data for marketing or value added services (Art 6(3))?
-- Purpose, prior consent, and limited to what is necessary: "may process ... if the subscriber or user ... has given his or her prior consent".
#ASSERT (`May my provider process my traffic data for marketing or value added services` WITH `it is for marketing electronic communications services or for a value added service` IS TRUE, `I gave my prior consent` IS TRUE, `the processing goes no further than the services or marketing need` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No consent: a "may" grant whose "if" gate failed; the text does not close the gate with "only".
#ASSERT (`May my provider process my traffic data for marketing or value added services` WITH `it is for marketing electronic communications services or for a value added service` IS TRUE, `I gave my prior consent` IS FALSE, `the processing goes no further than the services or marketing need` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I18: Can I withdraw my consent to the processing of my traffic data at any time (Art 6(3))?
-- Art 6(3): users or subscribers "shall be given the possibility to withdraw their consent ... at any time".
#ASSERT (`Can I withdraw my consent to the processing of my traffic data at any time` WITH `my consent was for processing traffic data under Art 6(3)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Consent for something else: the sentence is about traffic data.
#ASSERT (`Can I withdraw my consent to the processing of my traffic data at any time` WITH `my consent was for processing traffic data under Art 6(3)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I19: Has my provider told me what it must about my traffic data (Art 6(4))?
-- Told the types and the duration, and before consent where the processing needs consent.
#ASSERT (`Has my provider told me what it must about my traffic data` WITH `the processing is for marketing or a value added service` IS TRUE, `my provider told me the types of traffic data processed` IS TRUE, `my provider told me how long it processes them` IS TRUE, `my provider told me before it asked for my consent` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Told only after consent was obtained: "prior to obtaining consent".
#ASSERT (`Has my provider told me what it must about my traffic data` WITH `the processing is for marketing or a value added service` IS TRUE, `my provider told me the types of traffic data processed` IS TRUE, `my provider told me how long it processes them` IS TRUE, `my provider told me before it asked for my consent` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I20: Is the handling of my traffic data restricted as Art 6(5) requires?
-- Handled by persons under the provider's authority, for billing, and no further than necessary.
#ASSERT (`Is the handling of my traffic data restricted as Article 6(5) requires` WITH `it is handled by someone under the authority of my provider` IS TRUE, `the handling is for one of the listed activities` IS `billing`, `the handling goes no further than the activity needs` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Handled for another activity: Art 6(5) "must be restricted to" the listed activities.
#ASSERT (`Is the handling of my traffic data restricted as Article 6(5) requires` WITH `it is handled by someone under the authority of my provider` IS TRUE, `the handling is for one of the listed activities` IS `another activity`, `the handling goes no further than the activity needs` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `A few more rights as the person called or located (Articles 7 and 9)`
-- I58: I get itemised bills: must my privacy as a caller or called person be reconciled with that (Art 7(2))?
-- Art 7(2): Member States shall apply national provisions to reconcile the rights of subscribers receiving itemised bills with the privacy of calling users and called subscribers.
#ASSERT (`I get itemised bills: must the callers and called persons privacy be reconciled with that` WITH `I receive itemised bills` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No itemised bills: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`I get itemised bills: must the callers and called persons privacy be reconciled with that` WITH `I receive itemised bills` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I59: Must my provider tell me before asking my consent to location processing (Art 9(1))?
-- Prior to obtaining consent the provider must inform the users or subscribers.
#ASSERT (`Must my provider tell me before asking my consent to location processing` WITH `my provider is asking for my consent to location processing` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No consent is being obtained: the sentence is silent ("prior to obtaining their consent").
#ASSERT (`Must my provider tell me before asking my consent to location processing` WITH `my provider is asking for my consent to location processing` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I60: Once I have consented to location processing, must I be able to refuse it temporarily (Art 9(2))?
-- "Where consent ... has been obtained ... the user or subscriber must continue to have the possibility ... of temporarily refusing the processing".
#ASSERT (`Once I have consented to location processing must I be able to refuse it temporarily` WITH `I consented to location processing` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No consent obtained: the "where" condition fails (fork register F6).
#ASSERT (`Once I have consented to location processing must I be able to refuse it temporarily` WITH `I consented to location processing` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `More of the Directive's own terms and my other rights (Articles 2, 8, 10, 12 and 16)`
-- I61: Is this data "traffic data" under the Directive (Art 2(b))?
-- Processed to convey the communication: Art 2(b) "means".
#ASSERT (`Is this data traffic data under the Directive` WITH `it is processed to convey a communication on a network` IS TRUE, `it is processed for billing a communication` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Processed for billing: Art 2(b) "means".
#ASSERT (`Is this data traffic data under the Directive` WITH `it is processed to convey a communication on a network` IS FALSE, `it is processed for billing a communication` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither purpose: not traffic data.
#ASSERT (`Is this data traffic data under the Directive` WITH `it is processed to convey a communication on a network` IS FALSE, `it is processed for billing a communication` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I62: Is this data "location data" under the Directive (Art 2(c))?
-- Processed in a network and indicating the position of the terminal: Art 2(c) "means".
#ASSERT (`Is this data location data under the Directive` WITH `it is processed in a network` IS TRUE, `it is processed by a service` IS FALSE, `it shows where my device is` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- It does not indicate a position: not location data.
#ASSERT (`Is this data location data under the Directive` WITH `it is processed in a network` IS TRUE, `it is processed by a service` IS TRUE, `it shows where my device is` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I63: Is what I exchanged a "communication" under the Directive (Art 2(d))?
-- A finite number of parties, by a public service: Art 2(d) "means".
#ASSERT (`Is what I exchanged a communication under the Directive` WITH `it was exchanged between a finite number of parties` IS TRUE, `it went by a publicly available service` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not by a publicly available service: not a communication.
#ASSERT (`Is what I exchanged a communication under the Directive` WITH `it was exchanged between a finite number of parties` IS TRUE, `it went by a publicly available service` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I64: Can I hide my number on every call from my line, not call by call (Art 8(1))?
-- The possibility exists, per line.
#ASSERT (`Can I hide my number on every call from my line not call by call` WITH `I can prevent the presentation of my number` IS TRUE, `I can do it for the whole line` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The possibility is only per call: the sentence asks for per-line.
#ASSERT (`Can I hide my number on every call from my line not call by call` WITH `I can prevent the presentation of my number` IS TRUE, `I can do it for the whole line` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I65: Has my Member State ensured transparent procedures for overriding the hiding of my number (Art 10)?
-- A transparent procedure exists.
#ASSERT (`Has my Member State ensured transparent procedures for overriding the hiding of my number` WITH `there is a procedure governing how my provider may override` IS TRUE, `the procedure is transparent` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The procedure is not transparent: the Member State has not ensured what Art 10 asks.
#ASSERT (`Has my Member State ensured transparent procedures for overriding the hiding of my number` WITH `there is a procedure governing how my provider may override` IS TRUE, `the procedure is transparent` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I66: If my number is revealed to trace a malicious call, will my data be stored and made available (Art 10(a))?
-- After an override, the data are stored and made available in accordance with national law.
#ASSERT (`If my number is revealed to trace a malicious call will my data be stored and made available` WITH `my provider overrode the hiding of my number to trace a malicious call` IS TRUE, `the storing is in accordance with national law` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No override: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`If my number is revealed to trace a malicious call will my data be stored and made available` WITH `my provider overrode the hiding of my number to trace a malicious call` IS FALSE, `the storing is in accordance with national law` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I67: I am a company: must my legitimate interests about my directory entry be protected (Art 12(4))?
-- Not a natural person: the Member State must sufficiently protect the legitimate interests.
#ASSERT (`I am a company must my legitimate interests about my directory entry be protected` WITH `I am a natural person` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A natural person: paragraph 4 second sentence is about the other subscribers.
#ASSERT (`I am a company must my legitimate interests about my directory entry be protected` WITH `I am a natural person` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I68: Does the directory rule reach a directory edition that was already printed (Art 16(1))?
-- Produced in printed form before the national law took effect: Art 12 does not apply to it.
#ASSERT (`Does the directory rule reach a directory edition that was already printed` WITH `the edition was already produced or placed on the market` IS TRUE, `it is in printed or off-line electronic form` IS TRUE, `that was before the national law took effect` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not produced before: the sentence is silent about it.
#ASSERT (`Does the directory rule reach a directory edition that was already printed` WITH `the edition was already produced or placed on the market` IS FALSE, `it is in printed or off-line electronic form` IS TRUE, `that was before the national law took effect` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `My bill and my line identification (Articles 7 and 8)`
-- I21: Do I have the right to a non-itemised bill (Art 7(1))?
-- Art 7(1): subscribers have the right to receive non-itemised bills.
#ASSERT (`Do I have the right to a non-itemised bill` WITH `I am a subscriber` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a subscriber: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`Do I have the right to a non-itemised bill` WITH `I am a subscriber` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I22: Has my provider given me the possibility of hiding my number on a call I make (Art 8(1))?
-- Offered per call, by a simple means, free of charge.
#ASSERT (`Has my provider given me the possibility of hiding my number on a call I make` WITH `my provider lets me hide my number` IS TRUE, `I can do it call by call` IS TRUE, `it is simple to do` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not free of charge: "using a simple means and free of charge".
#ASSERT (`Has my provider given me the possibility of hiding my number on a call I make` WITH `my provider lets me hide my number` IS TRUE, `I can do it call by call` IS TRUE, `it is simple to do` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I23: When I am called, has my provider given me the possibility of hiding the caller's number from me (Art 8(2))?
-- Offered by a simple means, and free of charge for reasonable use.
#ASSERT (`Has my provider let me stop callers' numbers being shown to me` WITH `my provider lets me stop callers' numbers being shown to me` IS TRUE, `it is simple to do` IS TRUE, `my use of this is reasonable` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Unreasonable use: "free of charge for reasonable use" does not say it must be free then.
#ASSERT (`Has my provider let me stop callers' numbers being shown to me` WITH `my provider lets me stop callers' numbers being shown to me` IS TRUE, `it is simple to do` IS TRUE, `my use of this is reasonable` IS FALSE, `it is free` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I24: Can I reject calls whose caller has hidden their number (Art 8(3))?
-- Offered by a simple means.
#ASSERT (`Can I reject incoming calls whose caller has hidden their number` WITH `my provider lets me reject calls from hidden numbers` IS TRUE, `it is simple to do` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not offered: "must offer the called subscriber the possibility ... of rejecting incoming calls".
#ASSERT (`Can I reject incoming calls whose caller has hidden their number` WITH `my provider lets me reject calls from hidden numbers` IS FALSE, `it is simple to do` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I25: Can I stop my number being shown to the person who calls me when I answer (Art 8(4))?
-- Offered by a simple means, free of charge.
#ASSERT (`Can I stop my connected line identification being shown to the caller` WITH `my provider lets me hide who answers` IS TRUE, `it is simple to do` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not free of charge.
#ASSERT (`Can I stop my connected line identification being shown to the caller` WITH `my provider lets me hide who answers` IS TRUE, `it is simple to do` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I26: Does my right to hide my number also reach a call I make to another country (Art 8(5))?
-- Art 8(5): paragraph 1 "shall also apply" to calls to third countries originating in the Community.
#ASSERT (`Does my right to hide my number reach a call to another country` WITH `the call is to a country outside the Community` IS TRUE, `the call starts in the Community` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A call that does not originate in the Community: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`Does my right to hide my number reach a call to another country` WITH `the call is to a country outside the Community` IS TRUE, `the call starts in the Community` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I27: Do my rights as the person called also reach a call from another country (Art 8(5))?
-- Art 8(5): paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 "shall also apply to incoming calls originating in third countries".
#ASSERT (`Do my rights as the person called reach a call from another country` WITH `it is a call coming in to me` IS TRUE, `the call starts outside the Community` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A call from within the Community: this sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`Do my rights as the person called reach a call from another country` WITH `it is a call coming in to me` IS TRUE, `the call starts outside the Community` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Where my phone is (Article 9)`
-- I28: May my location data (other than traffic data) be processed (Art 9(1))?
-- Made anonymous: "may only be processed when they are made anonymous, or with the consent".
#ASSERT (`May my location data be processed` WITH `it is location data about me held by a public network or service` IS TRUE, `it has been made anonymous` IS TRUE, `I consented` IS FALSE, `the processing is limited to what the value added service needs` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither anonymous nor consented: the text closes the permission with "only".
#ASSERT (`May my location data be processed` WITH `it is location data about me held by a public network or service` IS TRUE, `it has been made anonymous` IS FALSE, `I consented` IS FALSE, `the processing is limited to what the value added service needs` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Consent, limited to what the value added service needs.
#ASSERT (`May my location data be processed` WITH `it is location data about me held by a public network or service` IS TRUE, `it has been made anonymous` IS FALSE, `I consented` IS TRUE, `the processing is limited to what the value added service needs` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I29: Has my provider told me what it must before asking my consent to location processing (Art 9(1))?
-- Told all four things before consent.
#ASSERT (`Has my provider told me what it must before asking my consent to location processing` WITH `my provider told me what type of location data` IS TRUE, `my provider told me the purposes` IS TRUE, `my provider told me how long` IS TRUE, `my provider told me whether a third party gets it` IS TRUE, `my provider told me before I consented` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not told whether a third party receives the data.
#ASSERT (`Has my provider told me what it must before asking my consent to location processing` WITH `my provider told me what type of location data` IS TRUE, `my provider told me the purposes` IS TRUE, `my provider told me how long` IS TRUE, `my provider told me whether a third party gets it` IS FALSE, `my provider told me before I consented` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I30: Can I withdraw my consent to location processing at any time (Art 9(1))?
-- The possibility is given.
#ASSERT (`Can I withdraw my consent to location processing at any time` WITH `I can withdraw my consent at any time` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not given: "shall be given the possibility to withdraw their consent ... at any time".
#ASSERT (`Can I withdraw my consent to location processing at any time` WITH `I can withdraw my consent at any time` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I31: Can I temporarily refuse the processing of my location for each connection (Art 9(2))?
-- All four elements present.
#ASSERT (`Can I temporarily refuse the processing of my location for each connection` WITH `I can temporarily refuse` IS TRUE, `it is simple to do` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS TRUE, `I can do it for each connection or each transmission` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not for each connection or transmission.
#ASSERT (`Can I temporarily refuse the processing of my location for each connection` WITH `I can temporarily refuse` IS TRUE, `it is simple to do` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS TRUE, `I can do it for each connection or each transmission` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Call forwarding and the directory (Articles 11 and 12)`
-- I32: Must I be able to stop automatic call forwarding to my line (Art 11)?
-- Art 11: any subscriber has the possibility of stopping automatic call forwarding by a third party to the subscriber's terminal.
#ASSERT (`Must I be able to stop automatic call forwarding to my line` WITH `I am a subscriber` IS TRUE, `calls are being forwarded to my line automatically by a third party` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not forwarding by a third party to the subscriber's terminal: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`Must I be able to stop automatic call forwarding to my line` WITH `I am a subscriber` IS TRUE, `calls are being forwarded to my line automatically by a third party` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I33: Must I be told about a directory before my details are put in it (Art 12(1))?
-- A public directory in which my data can be included: subscribers are informed before inclusion.
#ASSERT (`Must I be told about a directory before my details are put in it` WITH `it is a printed or electronic directory open to the public` IS TRUE, `my details could be put in it` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not such a directory: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`Must I be told about a directory before my details are put in it` WITH `it is a printed or electronic directory open to the public` IS FALSE, `my details could be put in it` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I34: Was I told what I must be told, free of charge, before I was put in the directory (Art 12(1))?
-- Told the purposes, the search functions, free of charge and before inclusion.
#ASSERT (`Was I told what I must be told before I was put in the directory` WITH `I was told the purposes of the directory` IS TRUE, `the directory has search functions in an electronic version` IS TRUE, `I was told what else those search functions allow` IS TRUE, `I was told free of charge` IS TRUE, `I was told before I was put in the directory` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Told only after inclusion.
#ASSERT (`Was I told what I must be told before I was put in the directory` WITH `I was told the purposes of the directory` IS TRUE, `the directory has search functions in an electronic version` IS TRUE, `I was told what else those search functions allow` IS TRUE, `I was told free of charge` IS TRUE, `I was told before I was put in the directory` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I35: Must I be able to decide whether and what of mine is in a public directory and to correct or withdraw it (Art 12(2))?
-- Art 12(2): subscribers are given the opportunity to determine inclusion and to verify, correct or withdraw.
#ASSERT (`Must I be able to decide what of mine is in a public directory` WITH `it is a public directory` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a public directory: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`Must I be able to decide what of mine is in a public directory` WITH `it is a public directory` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I36: Is not being in a public directory, and checking, correcting or withdrawing my data, free of charge for me (Art 12(2))?
-- All four free of charge.
#ASSERT (`Is not being in a public directory and correcting my data free of charge for me` WITH `not being included was free` IS TRUE, `verifying my data was free` IS TRUE, `correcting my data was free` IS TRUE, `withdrawing my data was free` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Correcting was charged for: "shall be free of charge".
#ASSERT (`Is not being in a public directory and correcting my data free of charge for me` WITH `not being included was free` IS TRUE, `verifying my data was free` IS TRUE, `correcting my data was free` IS FALSE, `withdrawing my data was free` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I37: Do the directory rights of paragraphs 1 and 2 reach me as a natural person (Art 12(4))?
-- Paragraphs 1 and 2 apply to subscribers who are natural persons.
#ASSERT (`Do the directory rights reach me as a natural person` WITH `I am a natural person` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a natural person: this sentence is silent (the second sentence deals with other subscribers).
#ASSERT (`Do the directory rights reach me as a natural person` WITH `I am a natural person` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `If my provider's network is attacked (Article 4)`
-- I38: Must my provider warn me of a particular risk to the security of the network (Art 4(2))?
-- In case of a particular risk the provider must inform the subscribers concerning it.
#ASSERT (`Must my provider warn me of a particular risk to the security of the network` WITH `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No such risk: "In case of a particular risk" is not met.
#ASSERT (`Must my provider warn me of a particular risk to the security of the network` WITH `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I39: Must my provider also tell me about a personal data breach that may harm me (Art 4(3))?
-- A breach likely to adversely affect me: the provider "shall also notify the subscriber or individual".
#ASSERT (`Must my provider also tell me about a personal data breach that may harm me` WITH `there has been a personal data breach` IS TRUE, `it is likely to harm my data or privacy` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A breach not likely to affect me adversely: the "when" gate fails.
#ASSERT (`Must my provider also tell me about a personal data breach that may harm me` WITH `there has been a personal data breach` IS TRUE, `it is likely to harm my data or privacy` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I40: Is my provider excused from telling me about the breach because it protected my data (Art 4(3))?
-- Excused: "shall not be required if the provider has demonstrated ... appropriate technological protection measures" that were applied and render the data unintelligible.
#ASSERT (`Is my provider excused from telling me about the breach because it protected my data` WITH `my provider showed the authority it had protective measures` IS TRUE, `those measures covered my data` IS TRUE, `they make my data unintelligible to anyone not authorised` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Measures that do not make the data unintelligible: the sentence says when notification is not required, not that it is required.
#ASSERT (`Is my provider excused from telling me about the breach because it protected my data` WITH `my provider showed the authority it had protective measures` IS TRUE, `those measures covered my data` IS TRUE, `they make my data unintelligible to anyone not authorised` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- I41: Does the notice I was sent about the breach say what it must (Art 4(3))?
-- Nature, contact points and recommended measures.
#ASSERT (`Does the breach notice I was sent say what it must` WITH `it describes the nature of the breach` IS TRUE, `it gives contact points` IS TRUE, `it recommends measures to limit the harm` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No contact points: "shall at least describe the nature ... and the contact points".
#ASSERT (`Does the breach notice I was sent say what it must` WITH `it describes the nature of the breach` IS TRUE, `it gives contact points` IS FALSE, `it recommends measures to limit the harm` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Unsolicited messages and calls: the recipient (Article 13)`
-- I42: May this marketing message be sent to me (Art 13)?
-- An e-mail I consented to beforehand, with nothing disguised: allowed.
#ASSERT (`May this marketing message be sent to me` WITH `the message reached me by` IS `an electronic mail message`, `the message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `I did not ask for the message` IS TRUE, `I am a natural person` IS TRUE, `I gave my consent beforehand` IS TRUE, `the sender got my details from me as its customer` IS FALSE, `I gave them when buying a product or service` IS TRUE, `I gave them lawfully under Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE, `the sender is the business I bought from` IS TRUE, `the message sells the sender's own products or services` IS TRUE, `the products or services are similar to what I bought` IS TRUE, `I was clearly and distinctly offered a way to object` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was free` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was easy` IS TRUE, `I was offered it when the details were collected` IS TRUE, `I refused at the start` IS FALSE, `I was offered it with every message` IS TRUE, `the sender's identity is disguised or concealed` IS FALSE, `the message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS FALSE, `there is no valid address to ask them to stop` IS FALSE, `the message pushes me to a website that breaks that Article` IS FALSE, `national law has chosen` IS `national legislation has not been stated`, `I do not wish to receive these messages` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
