-- National law's choice is outside the sources, and I gave no consent but have not said I do not wish to receive such calls: the first option prohibits it and the second does not, so the text does not decide it (fork F19).
#ASSERT (`Must national law make an unsolicited marketing call that is not an automatic call fax or e-mail not allowed` WITH `the call or message reached me by` IS `another means of communication`, `I did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `it is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `national law has chosen` IS `national legislation has not been stated`, `I gave my consent` IS FALSE, `I do not wish to receive them` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- National law's choice is outside the sources, and I consented but also do not wish to receive such calls: consent answers the first option and my objection the second, so the text does not decide it (fork F19).
#ASSERT (`Must national law make an unsolicited marketing call that is not an automatic call fax or e-mail not allowed` WITH `the call or message reached me by` IS `another means of communication`, `I did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `it is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `national law has chosen` IS `national legislation has not been stated`, `I gave my consent` IS TRUE, `I do not wish to receive them` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
